<!--Post: 3423--><!--Time: 1104887784-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3423"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 5:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Do you think BTK took some classes in college <BR>on how to develop Photo&#39;s? He took Picture that he sent to police right? So maybe on the same days he was in PJ&#39;s classes he also took a class on Photo&#39;s. Maybe the police could see if the same names match for a Photo class and a class PJ taught &amp; check out those people.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3423-->
<!--Post: 3428--><!--Time: 1104889297-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3428"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 5:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t believe we know BTK used anything besides an instant camera, although I could be wrong.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3428-->
<!--Post: 3438--><!--Time: 1104896240-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3438"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 7:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->True.  As far as I know, BTK used a polaroid.  But he WOULD use such a basic tool as his equipment may have been way to specifically built; would be easy to trace.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3438-->
<!--Post: 3468--><!--Time: 1104946752-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3468"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 9:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To me, this is one of the most intriguing aspects of this case. Do we know if the photos that he has sent to the WPD and news outlets are Polaroids, or from film? <BR> <BR>Mike Kelleher&#39;s profile mentions an interest in photography, which is built on the fact that BTK has lingered at some of the crime scenes for the express purpose of taking photographs of his work. He may have used a Polaroid to take some quick snapshots, but I would be willing to bet that he has used a film camera as well. Anybody with a serious interest in photography is going to use something better than a Polaroid, because film cameras produce better image quality. And since the photos are arguably some of his most prized souvenirs from his crimes, I would hazard to guess that image quality and durability are priorities for him. <BR> <BR>The Vian children reported that their mother&#39;s killer carried a bag with him. Could he possibly be bringing a kit with him to the crime scenes that includes camera equipment? <BR> <BR>Some have suggested that wherever BTK calls home has a darkroom for him to develop his crime scene photos - obviously, those particular rolls of film are not something he&#39;s going to send down to Wal-Mart for 1-hour processing. <BR> <BR>However, he doesn&#39;t necessarily have to have a darkroom to develop his photos. Way back in my days as a student journalist in college, our news staff would attend competitive events where all content was produced on the spot. Our photographers who participated brought with them all the chemicals they needed, photo paper, processing pans, and a small lamp with one of those darklights that you see used where film is being processed. And they would do everything in the bathroom of the Motel 6 we stayed at. The photos came out just fine. <BR> <BR>BTK doesn&#39;t need a darkroom. He could do it all in a bathroom at his house or apartment. What he will have, of course, are the chemicals, paper, and some consumer-use processing equipment that could be bought very easily and anonymously through mail order.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3468-->
<!--Post: 3475--><!--Time: 1104952078-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3475"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 11:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve seen many good ideas about what the &#34;440&#34; in post &#34;from BTK&#34; may be related to.  <BR>Just to add my two cents, it reminded me of an old polaroid camera my uncle had.  <BR><a href="http://www.rwhirled.com/landlist/pics/campics/440.jpg" target=_top>http://www.rwhirled.com/landlist/pics/campics/440. jpg</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3475-->
<!--Post: 3651--><!--Time: 1105083814-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3651"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Deedle<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Deedle<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 11:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I find it doubtful he would take polaroids and then send them in. I think it&#39;s pretty well understood that the pictures are a way for him to relive the experience. <BR>I have a darkroom in my house, I set it up in a spare bathroom and clean it up when I&#39;m done. I&#39;m a senior in high school and know at least 3 other people in my grade with darkrooms. It can be a little pricey &#40;old enlargers can be found for a little under 500, but they usually have something wrong with them&#41;, but I wouldn&#39;t be surprised if btk decided to invest in it. He could even have a darkroom without his friends knowing about it, since you can just put everything away when you&#39;re done.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3651-->
